      "description": "Independence Day (America's 250th Anniversary) observed, impacting consumer activity.",
      "details": "Independence Day, a federal holiday, celebrates the signing of the Declaration of Independence. In 2026, July 4th fell on a Saturday, so the federal holiday was observed on Friday, July 3rd. This typically leads to widespread closures, travel, and participation in celebrations like parades and fireworks. The 250th anniversary likely amplified these offline activities. Consumers are generally less engaged in online shopping for non-essential items during such major national holidays.",
